Twig on Gentoo
==============

dev-vcs/twig builds the renderer and preload from the tagged Twig sources.
It includes upstream's matching prebuilt Electron runtime because ::gentoo
does not provide that Electron version. Native npm build tools are supplied
by their locked upstream packages. This is not a source build of Chromium.
dev-vcs/twig-bin installs the completed upstream Linux release instead.
Both packages install /usr/bin/twig and cannot be installed together.

All npm archives are declared in SRC_URI and verified by the Gentoo Manifest.
The offline installer also checks the integrity values in package-lock.json.
Lifecycle scripts and automatic Electron downloads are disabled. The source
ebuild supports USE=test for upstream lint and local Git fixture tests. The
obsolete test of a missing private-monorepo installer is excluded; the other
foundation checks remain enabled.

Releases after 0.8.5 use FSL-1.1-ALv2. Review the installed LICENSE.md and
NOTICE.md before accepting this license: it restricts competing commercial
uses and grants Apache 2.0 rights two years after each version's release.
Version 0.8.5 remains all-rights-reserved; the new license is not retroactive.
Binary redistribution is restricted. Bundled dependencies retain their own
license notices.

Update through Portage, not the in-app updater introduced in 0.14.0. Upstream
detects /opt installations as Debian packages and offers a .deb installer.
Automatic update checks are opt-in; downloads require an explicit click.

The launcher keeps upstream's isolated fontconfig cache, needed when the host
fontconfig cache format is newer than the bundled Electron supports. Set
TWIG_SYSTEM_FONTCONFIG=1 to opt out. Chromium's sandbox requires unprivileged
user namespaces; the package does not install a setuid sandbox helper.

Documentation:
https://github.com/kitarasenka/twig/blob/twig-v0.14.0/README.md
https://github.com/kitarasenka/twig/releases/tag/twig-v0.14.0
https://github.com/kitarasenka/twig/blob/twig-v0.14.0/LICENSE.md
https://www.electronjs.org/docs/latest/tutorial/sandbox
https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/commands/npm-ci

Maintainers can regenerate the npm SRC_URI block in a fresh source tree with:
npm pkg delete devDependencies.electron devDependencies.electron-builder devDependencies.playwright
npm --offline --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund install --package-lock-only
node /path/to/overlay/dev-vcs/twig/files/npm-offline.mjs uris package-lock.json

This drops the unused release packagers and GUI smoke-test driver. npm prunes
the existing lock graph without updating the retained dependency versions.
